program loop_until

? `loop until COND do` runs till the condition holds (desugared to
? while-not): clearer than negating compound conditions by hand.
? Counter form `loop i:0 until COND do` counts from the start.

@ main ||:
	expected: []
	expected.push|"0"|
	expected.push|"1"|
	expected.push|"2"|
	expected.push|"0"|
	expected.push|"1"|

	n: 0
	loop until n is 3 do
		print|n|
		n = n + 1
	$
	loop i:0 until i is 2 do
		print|i|
	$
	print|expected|
$
